spec:
  grid: N x N square, N in 8-16 [observed]
  background: azure (8)
  colors: exactly {background, blue (1), magenta (6)} in input; output replaces magenta with orange (7)
  pixels:
    blue_pivots: 3-7 single blue pixels scattered on background
    magenta_sources: same count as blue pivots; each shares exactly one row or column with a blue pivot
  matching: one-to-one pairing of sources to pivots via shared row/col; must be globally unique (no ambiguous alternate matching)
  source_pivot_distance: Manhattan 1-4 per pair; mix of same-row (~30%) and same-col (~70%) alignments [observed]
  transformation:
    remove all magenta; for each (source, pivot) pair rotate source 90 degrees CCW around pivot
    CCW rotation of offset (dr, dc) becomes (-dc, dr); paint in-bounds target orange
    if rotated target is out of grid bounds, source simply disappears (0-2 OOB per puzzle)
  constraints:
    - all rotated in-bounds targets must land on background (no collisions with blue or other targets)
    - source directions relative to pivot vary (above/below/left/right all occur)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. pick N from 8-16; create N x N azure grid
    2. pick K pairs from 3-7; place K blue pivot pixels at random positions (no two sharing both row and col)
    3. for each pivot, choose a random CCW-rotation offset (dr, dc) with Manhattan distance 1-4
